-- title:
--   Frobenius on Fontaine's submodule lands in p L
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which the image of $p$ is a non-zero-divisor. Let $k$ be a commutative ring of characteristic $p$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra such that the structure map $\mathcal O \to k$ is surjective with kernel exactly the ideal generated by $p$, and let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-bialgebra that is flat as an $\mathcal O$-module. Write $A = k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R$ and let $\pi : \mathcal R \to A$ be the ring map underlying $r \mapsto 1 \otimes r$ (`Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`). Here [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p A`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234) is the direct limit, over $n$, of the additive subgroups `wittHom k p n A` of $W_n(A)$ consisting of those truncated Witt vectors $x$ with $\mathrm{map}(\Delta)(x) = \mathrm{map}(\iota_1)(x) + \mathrm{map}(\iota_2)(x)$ (comultiplication versus the two inclusions $A \to A \otimes_k A$), the transition maps being induced by the length-shift; `frobenius` is the additive endomorphism induced levelwise by `frobeniusFun`; and [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p π`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) is the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of classes represented by some $x \in$ `wittHom k p n A` whose underlying element of $W_n(A)$ lies in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer p n π`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76). The assertion: for $z$ in the Dieudonné module, if `frobenius` $z$ lies in `fontaineHodge k p π`, then there is $y$ in `fontaineHodge k p π` with `frobenius` $z = (p : \mathbb Z) \cdot y$.
--
--   This is part (i) of Fontaine's first theorem on finite commutative group schemes over Witt vectors, in the form $F(M) \cap L \subseteq p\,L$ for the Dieudonné module $M$ of the special fibre and Fontaine's submodule $L$; no finiteness of $\mathcal R$ and no antipode enter. It is used in the verification that the pair consisting of Fontaine's submodule and the Dieudonné module of the special fibre satisfies the Honda-system axioms, via [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_hondaSystem_L_eq_fontaineHodge).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_exists_mem_fontaineHodge_frobenius_eq_smul.lean

